Going to bump the docs

* Who is Nitin Raval? Is he a driver? If so, is he an active driver now?  {color:#ff991f}Nitin was a vehicle specialist with Bolt Drive (Carsharing), so yes, kind of a driver. When we were notified about him not having a valid DL we terminated the employement and he left the company some weeks ago. {color}
* I am not sure I understand the question “To whom was the vehicle handed over?”.
** [~accountid:712020:a3bb4a62-5032-469c-a2b9-4d5c5e6979d6] can you please clarify what is requested here? {color:#ff991f}They ask us who “allowed” him driving the car, who is responsible that he had access to the cars. {color}
* Regarding this one: Who checks the employees' driving licences? {color:#ff991f}This is done by Recruiters hiring for the job who received special training for this purpose.{color}
** Why didn’t we check the license then? Why was the person allowed to drive? Please provide a brief explanation - is this a mistake on our side?

{color:#ff991f}It was checked by Tomasz Iwański (who is no longer in the company) but the fake not spotted due to human error. {color}

Hi [~accountid:6411c587f1b529dfa98c0e66] ,

Regarding the process of the Ordinary Shareholders' meeting, I can confirm that our external counsel will complete the template themselves using our financial statements, which we need to share with them beforehand.

For the remaining questions, I've forwarded an email  to our external counsel (attached and transcribed for our records). You are cc'd. I will revert as soon as they reply.

Many thanks.



[^Bolt Mail - Bolt Services Py S.A. - Annual Shareholder's Meeting.pdf]

{color:#36b37e}_Dear Vanessa,_{color}

{color:#36b37e}_Please accept my apologies for the delayed response; it's been quite a busy period here at Bolt._{color}

{color:#36b37e}_The financial statements are still a work in progress. However, my colleagues in the accounting department would like to clarify a few points:_{color}

# {color:#36b37e}_We understand that the Informative Declaration of the Tax Profit Distribution must be submitted by June 14th. One of the requirements for this submission is the approval of the annual accounts by the Ordinary Shareholders' meeting. Is it feasible to hold two meetings: one to approve the preliminary financial statements and another for the approval of the final ones?_{color}
# {color:#36b37e}_We are puzzled by the discrepancy between the extended deadline for submitting the financial statements (extended to August from April by local authorities) and the requirement to approve the annual accounts by June to meet the Informative Declaration of the Tax Profit Distribution deadline. Could you please explain this inconsistency? If one deadline is extended, shouldn't the other one also be extended, given their close linkage?_{color}
# {color:#36b37e}_Is there any possibility of extending the deadline for the Informative Declaration of the Tax Profit Distribution? Furthermore, what are the implications if we fail to file this declaration by June 14th?_{color}

{color:#36b37e}_Your guidance on these matters would be greatly appreciated._{color}

{color:#36b37e}_Best regards,_{color}

Hi [~accountid:604b91443ab18c0068f95304] 

Here are my notes (in {color:#ff991f}orange{color}):

11. Garantien: Dieser Punkt sollte auf Gegenseitigkeit ausgelegt sein, also im Sinne von "Die Parteien geben keine...." oder "Die offenlegende Partei gibt keine...."
{color:#ff991f}This is OK to amend as suggested by them.{color}

12.1. "Diese Vereinbarung kann von keiner der Parteien ohne die vorherige schriftliche Zustimmung der anderen Partei abgetreten werden." den Zusatz ".., wobei die vorherige schriftliche Zustimmung für eine Abtretung durch eine Partei an ein verbundenes Unternehmen nicht erforderlich ist." möchten wir streichen.
{color:#ff991f}Removing this would mean that Bolt (but also the counterparty) won’t be able to assign the NDA to any of its affiliates without the written confirmation of the other party. For example, another Bolt entity can’t freely replace Bolt in the NDA, as this should be approved by the counterparty beforehand. I don’t see any substantive legal or practical issues with this - therefore removing the suggested part is OK.{color}

12.3. Als Vertragsrecht bevorzugen wir deutsches Recht mit Gerichtsstand München, da die Vereinbarung ja nur für den deutschen Raum gelten wird.
{color:#ff991f}German law and courts are OK to accept.{color}

12.5. Der Vertrag kann gerne zweisprachig sein, im Streitfall sollte aus o.a. Gründen aber die deutsche Sprachfassung maßgeblich sein.
{color:#ff991f}I assume the contract is originally drafted in English and the German side is a translation. If so, then this suggestion can’t be agreed with. The translated version can have inaccuracies, translation errors etc. and therefore it should not prevail over the original version.{color}

Unterzeichnung: bitte teilen Sie uns auch den Namen und die Adresse der für Bolt unterzeichnenden Person mit
{color:#ff991f}Can you share who is signing for Bolt?{color}

cache for processing menu items sync in {{MenuItemSyncService}} (city): 

* key: {{menu_sync_${cityId}_status}}
* value: {{pending}} / {{done}}
* WRITE / UPDATE → when syncing all menu items:
** all cities put to {{pending}}
** a cron reads {{pending}} cities
** (NOTE - it looks like all cities are processed at once ? - have a second look here)
* READ → when syncing all menu items



cache for processing menu items sync in {{MenuItemSyncService}} (already processed providers): 

* key: {{menu_sync_${cityId}_last_processed_ids}}
* value: provider ids
* WRITE / UPDATE → when handling menu updates within a city, as providers are processed, they are added here
* READ → before handling a city, providers to be processed are the ones fetched from provider api, and which are not in this list

cache for availability locking in {{ProviderAvailabilityCacheService}}

* key: {{`availability_${userId}_${cityId}_${providerId}`}}
* value: {{ProviderAvailabilityState}}
* WRITE / UPDATE → on {{/saveProviderAvailability}} for user, in {{ProviderAvailabilityService}}
* READ → in {{ProviderAvailabilityCacheService}}, when computing cache aware availability - {{ProviderCacheAwareAvailabilityMapUpdater}}, to be returned for fetched providers (ex. {{/findProvidersInUserRange}}[{{/v2}}])

(NOTE - might want to save / read from the same class)

*hey* [~accountid:61addb80b0b630006a695081] *please find below their newest comments regarding 5.1, 7.2, 4.23, 4.9 and early termination parts, their comments are in red/green, ours in black. Please pay attention to the last part about early termination.*

[^Northstar_3_Transfer Deed.doc]
[^Northstar_2_Common Charges.doc]
[^Northstar_4_Operating Rules.doc]

5.1 Can you confirm that common areas would not be included in the rent since we will not be using them? I believe that we should apply the same conditions for everyone and calculate the total area as indicated in the contract (if not renting the 1st floor, the common areas will be used). {color:#bf2600}We do not include the common area in the rent for the mentioned premises, but you will have to pay the general building fees since the systems serve all clients.{color}

could you please confirm what exact fees would be included for common areas? {color:#36b37e}Please find attached an annex to the lease agreement where all common charges are listed.{color}



7.2 Is there an option to extend the contract for 6 months or one year? {color:#bf2600}We do not apply an automatic renewal option unless it is an additional 3-5 year contract. Typically, we coordinate the contract renewal with all tenants in advance.{color}

can we add something like “_The Parties agree that at least 6 months before the end of the Agreement, Bolt will send the Landlord a notification to extend the Agreement for an additional 3 years on the terms and conditions set herein. If no such notification is sent, the Agreement ends as stated in this Agreement._” {color:#36b37e}Yes, agreed.{color}



4.23 Can you explain in more detail when we would pay double rent? {color:#bf2600}This clause does not apply as the building has already been handed over and is 100% complete.{color}

Can we delete this part? {color:#36b37e}We can delete the part related to the commisionning of the building.{color}



4.9 Can you clarify what "Fit out" installations are being referred to? T{color:#bf2600}he premises are taken "as-is," so this clause does not apply. It would apply if the landlord made significant investments in the premises.{color}

Can we delete this part? {color:#36b37e}Yes, the landlord will not carry out any fit-out works and handover the premises „as-is“.{color}



What is the penalty if the contract needs to be terminated before 3 years? {color:#bf2600}Typically, we do not grant the right to terminate the contract early because we would incur additional costs. Lithuanian courts have indicated that in the case of early termination, the typical penalty is 6 months' rent. We can include in the contract that if the tenant terminates the contract of their own will, a 6-month rent penalty would be paid. The premises are really in demand in the market, so we cannot fully agree to the early termination option.{color}

This is (very) common on the LT market - can we add this to the contract - six months rent penalty. {color:#36b37e}Unfortunately, the lease is too short to add additionally a termination notice, otherwise we could consider alternative tenants with no termination option and longer leases.The parties can always negotiate if there are any turbulances. Hopefully, we can agree to keep the 3 year contract.  {color}

The point about early termination is unclear because you previously mentioned that according to Lithuanian laws, if a tenant moves out, a six-month rent amount is applied. As I understand it, we cannot include this in the contract, but if this were to happen, would this law still apply?

Of course, we don't want or plan for this, but we need to consider all options.

{color:#36b37e}This is the practice of Lithuanian courts. It is unlikely that the parties would go to court if they agreed on a 6-month penalty because the probability of receiving more is only theoretical. It is important for us not to have such conditions, not because we wouldn't accept 6 months, but because the financing bank requires non-terminable contracts. In practice, all contracts are terminated with a certain penalty amount.{color}

