To followup on the call [~accountid:712020:47b28358-3e16-42e1-98f8-60975dca1fc0] :

* the activity is in ideation phase and even no tests were performed;
* privacy will check the PN next week to find any provisions that may cover the activity;
* in case there is a relevant PN provision, the activity can be commenced with no risk. Identifying influencers and reaching out to them is also possible;
* in case there is no transparency for the data subjects, the activity cannot be done until transparency is ensured. Proceeding without prior notice to data subjects is medium privacy risk. Practical risks (i.e. data subjects not expecting this activity or being annoyed) must also be taken into account;
* an LIA will have to be completed by the privacy team to legalise the activity.

Privacy will get back to this next week after dealing with urgent regulatory matters.

