{panel:bgColor=#fffae6}
*Do we provide information on data breaches to users?*
{panel}

While I don’t think that requesting information about the fact that a data breach has happened is part of Art 15, I do believe that *we can inform the rider that we have no record of any data breaches that affected him.*

I nevertheless suggest treating requests about data breaches as ad-hoc - we are not obligated to disclose this information, but we also have no [commercial] reason to _not_ disclose it, especially when we have no record of a breach happening. 

To sum up, I think mentioning that we have no record of breaches affecting this rider is more beneficial for us than pushing back on this request - we might sound like we are trying to hide something if we push back.

